-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-- Kaushalya Developmental Screening Platform — item bank becomes sole source
--
-- 0006_item_bank.sql deliberately kept item_overrides as a diff on top of
-- content/items.ts: the shipped TypeScript file stayed the reviewable source
-- of truth, and this table only recorded what an admin changed.
--
-- That two-tier design is retired. From here on item_overrides is not a diff
-- — it is the entire question bank. content/items.ts stops being read by the
-- assessment, the scoring engine or the admin item-bank page at runtime; it
-- remains in the repo only as the historical transcription that seeded this
-- migration and as test fixture data (see tests/scoring.test.ts).
--
-- This migration inserts every question content/items.ts shipped, as a full,
-- ordinary row — not a diff entry — so nothing a parent could previously be
-- asked disappears the moment the code stops reading that file. `ON CONFLICT
-- DO NOTHING` means an id that already has a row (an admin edited or retired
-- it before this migration ran) keeps that admin's version untouched.
-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

on conflict (id) do nothing;
